# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# In QEMU: the network stack PD
# against a hostile NIC driver. The PDs start in priority order: the timer,
# seed_source, driver_stand_in, then the stack. The stack's first frame is a
# DHCP discover; the stand-in then passes back its bad frames.
NOWAYOS: timer: starting
NOWAYOS: net-stack-test seed_source: starting
NOWAYOS: net-stack-test seed_source: a fixed test seed sent on the stack's seed ring
NOWAYOS: net-stack-test driver_stand_in: starting
NOWAYOS: net-stack: starting
NOWAYOS: net-stack: seeded; interface up at 52:54:00:12:34:56: asking for a DHCP lease
NOWAYOS: net-stack-test driver_stand_in: the stack asks for a lease: a DHCP discover from 52:54:00:12:34:56
NOWAYOS: net-stack-test driver_stand_in: took 128 receive buffers; passed back 7 descriptors: 2 oversize frames, 3 malformed and 2 frames smoltcp cannot use
# AC 4: each oversize and malformed frame dropped and counted, without a
# panic, and nothing else counted as dropped (that frames passing the checks
# reach smoltcp is tested on the host, in nowayos-ip).
NOWAYOS: net-stack: dropped so far: 2 oversize frames, 3 malformed frames, 0 corrupt queue indices, 0 frames unsent

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match),
# including in the second after the last line above: a fault reported by the
# Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic, a PD giving up, the
# stack not ready or failing to read the time, or a lease - nothing here
# offers one.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!not ready
!could not
!net-stack: DHCP lease
